# Line endings.
#
# Every text blob in this repository is already stored with LF, but nothing declared it, so
# the working tree was left to `core.autocrlf`. On Windows that checks files out as CRLF
# while the toolchain writes LF -- gofmt and Prettier both emit LF unconditionally -- so
# `make lint` rewrote every Go file's line endings and left ~130 files looking modified.
#
# Declaring it here makes the checkout match what the tools produce, on every platform and
# regardless of each developer's `core.autocrlf`. No renormalisation is needed: the stored
# blobs are LF already.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts have to keep CRLF to run.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never convert, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
